      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Erneut versuchen"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Search languages": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Sprachen suchen"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Measured end to end": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Durchgängig geprüft"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Everything else the engine knows": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Alle weiteren unterstützten Sprachen"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "German, English, Russian, and Ukrainian are measured end to end: recognition, cleanup, and every mark the review can show. The rest are recognized, and the marks that are calibrated per language stay off rather than guess.": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Deutsch, Englisch, Russisch und Ukrainisch sind durchgängig geprüft: Erkennung, Bereinigung und alle Hinweise der Überprüfung. Andere Sprachen werden erkannt; sprachabhängige Hinweise bleiben dort deaktiviert, statt Vermutungen anzuzeigen."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Preferred": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bevorzugt"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The preferred language decides a short phrase that could be either — “okay”, “ja”, a name on its own. A sentence long enough to be recognized is decided by what was said, not by this.": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die bevorzugte Sprache entscheidet bei kurzen, mehrdeutigen Äußerungen – etwa „okay“, „ja“ oder einem einzelnen Namen. Bei längeren Sätzen entscheidet das Gesprochene selbst."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Raw transcript, exactly as recognized": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Rohtranskript, genau wie erkannt"
